    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105720",
      "sequence": 2,
      "source_sequence": 2,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Behavioral responses to inheritance taxes: Evidence from Brazil",
      "title_cn": "对遗产税的行为反应：来自巴西的证据",
      "authors": [
        "Gedeão Locks"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "I examine behavioral responses to inheritance and gift taxes in a setting where individuals knew the tax would increase three months before the new tax code took effect. Using tax microdata from Brazil, I employ bunching and difference-in-differences (DD) methods and find that individuals significantly retime their wealth transfers to avoid taxes. Retimed gifts resulted in smaller inheritances for nearly three years. Moreover, I find that responses are sensitive to changes in top gift marginal tax rates and tax design (flat rates vs progressive brackets). Finally, evasion increased in the medium run in reform states, particularly among small inheritances.",
      "abstract_cn": "我研究了在新税法生效前几个月，个人就知道税收会增加的情况下对继承税和赠与税的行为反应。使用巴西的税收微观数据，我采用了聚类和双重差分 (DD) 方法，发现个人会大幅调整财富转移的时间来避税。重新安排捐赠时间导致近三年的遗产减少。此外，我发现反应对最高赠品边际税率和税收设计（统一税率与累进税率）的变化很敏感。最后，在改革国家中，逃税行为在中期有所增加，特别是在小额遗产中。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105720",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0047272726001568?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
