    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105733",
      "sequence": 9,
      "source_sequence": 9,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Do ultra-poor graduation programs build women’s resilience to weather shocks? Evidence from rural Ethiopia",
      "title_cn": "极端贫困的毕业项目能否增强女性抵御气候冲击的能力？来自埃塞俄比亚农村的证据",
      "authors": [
        "Kalle Hirvonen",
        "Daniel O. Gilligan",
        "Jessica Leight",
        "Heleene Tambet",
        "Victor Villa"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We assess whether layering an ultra-poor graduation program on Ethiopia’s Productive Safety Net Programme (PSNP) protects women and their households from localized weather shocks. Using panel data from a large cluster-randomized trial matched with detailed weather records, we identify community-level exposure to dryness shocks. Women who are exposed to dryness shocks experience deteriorating nutritional status (in conjunction with declining household food security and assets) and a significant increase in the risk of intimate partner violence. However, access to the graduation program fully buffers women from any increase in intimate partner violence, and partially buffers women and their households against other adverse effects. Further analysis suggests that improved household savings likely drives the program’s protective impact.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们评估在埃塞俄比亚的生产安全网计划（PSNP）中加入超贫困毕业计划是否可以保护妇女及其家庭免受局部天气冲击。利用大型集群随机试验的面板数据与详细的天气记录相匹配，我们确定了社区层面遭受干旱冲击的程度。遭受干旱冲击的妇女营养状况恶化（同时家庭粮食安全和资产下降），并且亲密伴侣暴力的风险显着增加。然而，参加毕业计划可以充分缓冲妇女免受亲密伴侣暴力增加的影响，并部分缓冲妇女及其家庭免受其他不利影响。进一步的分析表明，家庭储蓄的增加可能会推动该计划的保护作用。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105733",
