    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105735",
      "sequence": 11,
      "source_sequence": 11,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Implicit land taxes and their effect on the real economy",
      "title_cn": "隐性土地税及其对实体经济的影响",
      "authors": [
        "Daniel Murphy",
        "Nathan Seegert"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Land taxes are widely viewed as an efficient source of public revenue, yet explicit land taxation is rarely implemented. We study a closely related but largely overlooked object: implicit land taxes that arise within standard property tax systems when tax assessments place different relative weights on land and structures than market valuations do. Using parcel-level data on assessed values and transaction prices from U.S. counties, we estimate these implicit land taxes by comparing assessor and market hedonic valuations. We find substantial dispersion in implicit land taxes across and within metropolitan areas. Counties with higher implicit land taxes experience faster growth in population density, business establishments, earnings, and demographic diversity. These patterns are consistent with theoretical predictions that taxing land more heavily than structures encourages denser and more productive development.",
      "abstract_cn": "土地税被广泛视为公共收入的有效来源，但明确的土地税很少实施。我们研究一个密切相关但在很大程度上被忽视的对象：当税收评估对土地和结构的相对权重与市场估值不同时，标准财产税体系中就会产生隐性土地税。我们利用美国各县的评估值和交易价格的地块级数据，通过比较评估者和市场特征估值来估计这些隐含土地税。我们发现大都市地区之间和大都市地区内的隐性土地税存在很大的分散性。隐性土地税较高的县的人口密度、商业机构、收入和人口多样性增长较快。这些模式与理论预测相一致，即对土地征税比对建筑物征税更重会鼓励更密集、更高效的发展。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jpubeco.2026.105735",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0047272726001714?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
